	<EnglishText>
	<!-- Maps: Climate, Natural Wonder and Terrain settings -->
		<Row Tag="LOC_GROUPID_BBM_TERRAINOPTIONS"><Text>Terrain Settings</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_GROUPID_BBM_NATURALWONDERSELECTIONOPTIONS"><Text>Natural Wonder Selection</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LESS_NAME"><Text>Less</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MORE_NAME"><Text>More</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_HALF_NAME"><Text>Half</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_DOUBLE_NAME"><Text>Double</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_AGE_NAME"><Text>Map Age</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_AGE_DESC"><Text>Sets how broken the land is.[n]Mountains are set separately, so this moves ground only between flat and rough.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_AGE_OLD_DESC"><Text>Worn-down land, with less rough ground and broader plains.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_AGE_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>Standard terrain for the chosen map type.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_AGE_NEW_DESC"><Text>Freshly buckled land, with more rough ground and less flat.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_NAME"><Text>Map Temperature</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_DESC"><Text>Sets how warm the world is: which biomes cover the land, how far sea ice, reefs, and snow reach, and how strongly highlands, rainfall, and rivers change the local climate.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_FRIGID_NAME"><Text>Frigid</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_COLD_NAME"><Text>Cold</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_HOT_NAME"><Text>Hot</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_SCORCHING_NAME"><Text>Scorching</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_FRIGID_DESC"><Text>An ice-age world: about 70% of the land is tundra, sea ice and snow reach the middle latitudes, and river valleys hold most of the warm land.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_COLD_DESC"><Text>Tundra begins closer to the equator and desert gives way to grassland. Sea ice and snow reach further from the poles, and highlands turn to tundra sooner.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>Standard climate for the chosen map type.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_HOT_DESC"><Text>Desert reaches further from the equator and tundra retreats toward the poles. Sea ice and snow shrink, and rainy ground and river valleys turn greener.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_SCORCHING_DESC"><Text>A greenhouse world: desert and jungle cover most of the land, sea ice and snow vanish, and rivers become fertile strips through the desert.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_TEMPERATURE_RANDOM_DESC"><Text>One of the five temperatures, rolled from the map seed.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_NAME"><Text>Map Zones</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_DESC"><Text>Where the map's hot and cold regions lie.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>A hot band across the middle of the map, cooling toward the top and bottom, as in the base game.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_POLES_NAME"><Text>Hot Poles</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_POLES_DESC"><Text>Hot along the top and bottom of the map, with a cold band across the middle.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_EDGE_NAME"><Text>Hot Edge</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_EDGE_DESC"><Text>Hot along the north or south edge of the map, chosen by the map seed, cooling steadily to a frozen opposite edge.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_CENTER_NAME"><Text>Hot Center</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_HOT_CENTER_DESC"><Text>Hottest in the middle of the map, cooling outward in every direction, so the edges and corners are coldest.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_COLD_CENTER_NAME"><Text>Cold Center</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_COLD_CENTER_DESC"><Text>Coldest in the middle of the map, warming outward in every direction, so the edges and corners are hottest.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_WARM_RING_NAME"><Text>Warm Ring</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_WARM_RING_DESC"><Text>A warm ring circles the middle of the map, with cold at its center and around the edges.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_PATCHWORK_NAME"><Text>Patchwork</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_PATCHWORK_DESC"><Text>Hot and cold regions lie in irregular patches instead of bands.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MAP_ZONES_RANDOM_DESC"><Text>One of the seven layouts, rolled from the map seed.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_NAME"><Text>Natural Wonders</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_DESC"><Text>Sets the number of [icon:NOTIFICATION_DISCOVER_NATURAL_WONDER] Natural Wonders on the map.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_NONE_DESC"><Text>No Natural Wonders are placed.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_HALF_DESC"><Text>50% fewer Natural Wonders.[nn][BLIST][LI]Tiny: 1[LI]Small: 2[LI]Standard: 2[LI]Large: 3[LI]Huge: 3[/BLIST]</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>The standard number of Natural Wonders.[nn][BLIST][LI]Tiny: 3[LI]Small: 4[LI]Standard: 5[LI]Large: 6[LI]Huge: 7[/BLIST]</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_MORE_DESC"><Text>50% more Natural Wonders.[nn][BLIST][LI]Tiny: 4[LI]Small: 6[LI]Standard: 7[LI]Large: 9[LI]Huge: 10[/BLIST]</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDERS_DOUBLE_DESC"><Text>Twice as many Natural Wonders.[nn][BLIST][LI]Tiny: 6[LI]Small: 8[LI]Standard: 10[LI]Large: 12[LI]Huge: 14[/BLIST]</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDER_DESC"><Text>Whether this Natural Wonder can appear on the map.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDER_ON_DESC"><Text>This Natural Wonder can appear on the map.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_NATURAL_WONDER_OFF_DESC"><Text>This Natural Wonder is kept off the map.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LAKES_NAME"><Text>Lakes</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LAKES_DESC"><Text>Sets how many lakes the map generates.[n]Map generation may override this, so results can vary.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LAKES_LESS_DESC"><Text>Generates fewer lakes.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LAKES_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>Standard lake generation for the chosen map type.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_LAKES_MORE_DESC"><Text>Generates more lakes.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_NAME"><Text>Rivers</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_DESC"><Text>Sets how many rivers are generated and what share of them are Navigable Rivers rather than Minor Rivers.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_WADI_NAME"><Text>Wadis</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_WADI_DESC"><Text>50% fewer rivers, with far fewer of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_ARID_NAME"><Text>Arid</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_ARID_DESC"><Text>50% fewer rivers, with the usual share of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_CHANNEL_NAME"><Text>Channels</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_CHANNEL_DESC"><Text>50% fewer rivers, with far more of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_SHALLOW_NAME"><Text>Shallow</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_SHALLOW_DESC"><Text>The usual number of rivers, with far fewer of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>The usual number of rivers, with the usual share of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_WATERWAY_NAME"><Text>Waterways</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_WATERWAY_DESC"><Text>The usual number of rivers, with far more of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_STREAM_NAME"><Text>Streams</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_STREAM_DESC"><Text>50% more rivers, with far fewer of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_RIVERLAND_NAME"><Text>Riverlands</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_RIVERLAND_DESC"><Text>50% more rivers, with the usual share of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_DEEP_NAME"><Text>Deep</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_RIVERS_DEEP_DESC"><Text>50% more rivers, with far more of them navigable.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MOUNTAINS_NAME"><Text>Mountains</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MOUNTAINS_DESC"><Text>Sets how many mountains are generated when the map is created.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MOUNTAINS_LESS_DESC"><Text>Generates fewer mountains.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MOUNTAINS_STANDARD_DESC"><Text>Standard mountain generation for the chosen map type.</Text></Row>
		<Row Tag="LOC_BBM_MAPS_MOUNTAINS_MORE_DESC"><Text>Generates more mountains.</Text></Row>
